  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GRASSLAND MANAGEMENT FOR REPLENISHING HABITATS TO BOOST CONSERVATION OF RHINO AND TIGER IN MANAS NATIONAL PARK AND POBITORA WILDLIFE SANCTUARY IN ASSAM, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONSERVE AND RESTORE GRASSLAND HABITAT FOR THE SURVIVAL OF GRASSLAND DEPENDENT THREATENED SPECIES, SUCH AS THE GREATER ONE HORNED RHINO, HOG DEER, SWAMP DEER, HISPID HARE, PYGMY HOG, ASIATIC WATER BUFFALO, TIGER, ELEPHANT, BENGAL FLORICAN, SWAMP FRANCOLIN, AND ACT AS A MODEL FOR GRASSLAND RESTORATION ACROSS THE REGION. THE OBJECTIVES ARE TO (1) UNDERSTAND THE CURRENT STATUS AND DISTRIBUTION OF INVASIVE PLANTS SPECIES AND IDENTIFY THE PRIMARY DRIVERS OF THEIR INVASION IN POBITORA WILDLIFE SANCTUARY (2) IMPLEMENT AND VALIDATE APPROPRIATE INVASIVE SPECIES CONTROL METHODS IN POBITORA WILDLIFE SANCTUARY (3) CONTINUE THE MONITORING OF INVASIVE SPECIES IN THE GRASSLAND ECOSYSTEM OF MANAS NATIONAL PARK (MNP) AND RESTORE 20 SQ KM OF INVADED GRASSLAND (4) BUILD CAPACITY OF FRONTLINE STAFF IN RHINO BEARING AREAS ON GRASSLAND HABITAT MANAGEMENT (5) PROMOTE USES OF INVASIVE SPECIES FOR ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOOD THROUGH COORDINATION WITH AND SUPPORT FOR SELF HELP GROUPS IN EASTERN MANAS AND (6) REDUCE GRASSLAND DEGRADATION AND INCURSION IN MNP THROUGH THE PILOTING AND PROMOTION OF ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS AND IMPROVEMENT IN LIVESTOCK HUSBANDRY PRACTICES AND LIVESTOCK VACCINATION, IN COORDINATION WITH THE ECO DEVELOPMENT COMMITTEES IN CENTRAL MANAS.</narrative>
  </description>
